hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22682","Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from one who narrated to him, from Amr ibn Abd Allah ibn Ka'b, from the woman of those who pledged allegiance, that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us with his companions among Banu Salamah, so we brought near to him food, and he ate with his companions; then we brought near to him water for ablution, so he performed ablution, then turned to his companions and said: Shall I not inform you of the expiators of sins? They said: Yes indeed. He said: Perfecting ablution over disliked things, many steps to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer."
